   "evidence": "Statement at LightConeProjectors.lean:664-667; `L` occurs only in the hypothesis `hp : L.plus p \u2260 0`. The ingredients for the general version exist: `mem_transverse_minkowskiAxis_iff` (Relativity/LightConeBasis.lean:147), `minkowskiAxis` (ibid. 105), `plus_swap` (Mathematics/.../LightConeBasis.lean:275), and `timeComponent`/`spatialPart` are literally the coordinates `v (Sum.inl 0)` / `v (Sum.inr i)` (upstream/Physlib/.../Vector/Basic.lean:335,383).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Fermions/Dirac/LightConeProjectors.lean",
   "fix": "Keep this as the stepping stone and add the frame-free form outside the `LightConeBasis` namespace (e.g. in `Fermion.Dirac`): `(hshell : \u27eap, p\u27eb\u2098 = m ^ 2) (hp : p \u2260 0) \u2192 finrank \u2102 (ker (gammaMatrix p - m \u2022 1)) = 2`. The derivation is short with what the PR already has: if for every `i` both `(minkowskiAxis i).plus p = 0` and `(minkowskiAxis i).minus p = 0`, then `mem_transverse_minkowskiAxis_iff` gives `p.timeComponent = 0` and `p.spatialPart i = 0` for all `i`, hence `p = 0`; otherwise apply the present theorem to `minkowskiAxis i` or to its `swap` (`plus_swap : L.swap.plus = L.minus`).",
   "issue": "`finrank_ker_gammaMatrix_sub_smul_one_eq_two (hshell : \u27eap, p\u27eb\u2098 = m ^ 2) (hp : L.plus p \u2260 0) : finrank \u2102 (ker (gammaMatrix p - m \u2022 1)) = 2` has a conclusion that does not mention `L` at all; the light-cone basis and the frame-dependent `L.plus p \u2260 0` are artifacts of the proof route. The frame-free fact (`p \u2260 0` on the mass shell) is strictly more general and is what a user wants: as stated, counting solutions at a momentum first requires exhibiting a light-cone basis in which `p\u207a \u2260 0`.",
   "line": "664"
  }
 ],
